{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=8$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-8-(-3) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb232882e0ec631ab0725c2e2c840fff5ff45fb40276cb70e14a6ce35208b22f"} {"question" "q-124181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-11"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "Impossible to determine"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=16$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -16 & =-11+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -5 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb232882e0ec631ab0725c2e2c840fff5ff45fb40276cb70e14a6ce35208b22f"} {"question" "q-124186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-27"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "27"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/assets/1c074157bb6374a4da01d6c1312bb60520966317b1f903eb44a191384e398ae6.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of a quarter circle of radius $3$ and a line segment, as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{1}=1$ and ${y}_{2}=-4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=(-4)-1=-5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb232882e0ec631ab0725c2e2c840fff5ff45fb40276cb70e14a6ce35208b22f"} {"question" "q-124341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "3\\pi +2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the closed path along a circle of radius $2,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${y}_{1}={y}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb232882e0ec631ab0725c2e2c840fff5ff45fb40276cb70e14a6ce35208b22f"} {"question" "q-124346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "4"] ["math" "4\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e2402d53488631d5992e5e05c69ae8c6390ed36aa4de3574423dc7667d10fa"} {"question" "q-124349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066680/assets/0da125535534cbd50b96cb280cf8b8a4b58653a344c8